 "case": "N20-VALIDATION-NEG",
 "says": "A knowledge source is registered and two revisions are committed, each on the head the step before it moved to, the second correcting the rate table. A validation request pins both revisions and one lens; the validator checks only the first, so the run the owner records is unverified (partial_run) and its checks name the first revision as ran and the second as not run, never a clean verdict over part of what was pinned. A second request pins only the second revision under the same lens; the run finds a problem and records one check and one finding, both on that revision under that lens, naming no target or lens the request did not pin. A third request on the second revision times out and is recorded unverified. Every validation_run the owner writes here covers exactly the targets and lenses its request pinned (C12/validation_covers_its_request); the breaking records stay in the rule fixture.",
